# UTF-8 file writes (Windows)

Never write source/config/scripts as UTF-16. UTF-16 breaks Vite/esbuild, PowerShell (`.ps1`), SQL, and Cloudflare Pages deploys.

## Required

1. After **any new file** created with Write (especially `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.ps1`, `.sql`), verify first bytes are normal ASCII (not `47,0` / null-interleaved, not `255,254` UTF-16 LE BOM).
2. If UTF-16 is detected, rewrite immediately:
   ```powershell
   [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($path, $text, [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))
   ```
3. For **`.ps1` / `.bat` / `.cmd`**, never use PowerShell `Set-Content` / `Out-File` without UTF-8 no-BOM.
4. Run `npm run build` before pushing LIMS UI changes when a new source file was added in the same change set.

## Do not

- Ship a commit that contains UTF-16 source (Cloudflare Pages will fail with `Expected ";" but found "\x00"`)
- Re-save the same file multiple times "to fix encoding" without verifying bytes